From: VCKing101 <59761021+VCKing101@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 08:54:29 +1030
Subject: [PATCH 61/62] Disc: read the image through in the background from
 launch

A thread reads the whole disc image once at the system's background I/O
priority (Windows) and throws the bytes away, so the file cache holds it by
the time the game reads; a game's synchronous reads from its main loop no
longer stall a frame on a cold hard drive. Not started for an image larger
than half the machine's memory. <prefix>_NO_DISC_READ_THROUGH turns it off.
<prefix>_TRACE_IO now gives each read's time and whether it was asynchronous.

Measured on Dissidia 012 with a cold cache on a 5400 rpm drive: the battle's
first music block 85 ms -> 11.5 ms, the first battle frame 116 -> 47 ms.
Not checked: the Steam Deck (no lower I/O priority on Linux).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
